nal_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2019-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "D563BD67B80FF6A76C0E6BFE3940E17C", "name": "Travel with Hemant", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Vacationer710067", "username": "Vacationer710067", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1c/01/cf/b1/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 274, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293860, "location_name": "India", "location_name_detailed": "India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/1b/ac/b6/photo0jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/1b/ac/b7/photo1jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/1b/ac/b8/photo2jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2019-11-23", "published_at_date": "2019-11-23"}, {"review_id": 727999511, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r727999511-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Worth a visit", "text": "Rather a ramshackled group of temples, but most interesting and a unique experience for foreigners like us.  We witnessed the actual cremations of deceased Hindus, which was a rather peculiar experience, certainly for us.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "335B55D809044581F5CDF3116021EC59", "name": "Worldwatcher", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Worldwatcher", "username": "Worldwatcher", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-l/01/2a/fd/9f/avatar.jpg", "contribution_count": 1059, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 155019, "location_name": "Toronto", "location_name_detailed": "Toronto, Canada"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-11-21", "published_at_date": "2019-11-21"}, {"review_id": 727738794, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r727738794-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Padhupatinath", "text": "Nothing like this in the Western world. As a tourist it is great to visit a place like this, however very strange to be a part of such intimate life-events of the local people.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "6F54ECF94AAB6A9074DB3FF090C3CE35", "name": "Rianne", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/rianneforeveryoung", "username": "rianneforeveryoung", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/de/5a/default-avatar-2020-36.jpg", "contribution_count": 9, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-11-20", "published_at_date": "2019-11-20"}, {"review_id": 727207004, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r727207004-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A sacred place for Hindus; can't be in Kathmandu and miss it", "text": "We had hired a cab and Pashupati Nath was one of the attractions for the day. We visited just about it was closing in the afternoon and hence a piece of advice: The temple is closed between 2-5 p.m. We did make it in nick of time. The main temple offers views from all four sides and we managed most. Photography is strictly prohibited. Nearby are 522 \"shiv lings\" and you criss-cross them a riveting experience. Architecture is splendid and you sense a history around this huge complex. Wish Bagmati River, which flows alongside was cleaner and not clogged. It's also a place for cremation for it's believed you wash off all your sins if your body is put on pyre here.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "05F07E0F9C5C199C4E32065444BA3A73", "name": "ashishs474", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/ashishs474", "username": "ashishs474", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/10/33/e0/ashishs474.jpg", "contribution_count": 7, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 644043, "location_name": "Noida", "location_name_detailed": "Noida, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-11-18", "published_at_date": "2019-11-18"}, {"review_id": 727202837, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r727202837-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Ancient Holy Hindu temple", "text": "Interested in seeing this ancient ramshackle Hindu temple, I took a taxi here from the domestic airport (for Rs400) and paid another Rs1000 to enter. I declined a guide. \n\nIt was at the time of a traditional cremation ceremony, so it was quite crowded by the Bagmati river bank. The river is very polluted. There were bonfires burning as part of the ceremony.\n\nI didn’t have a map or guide book so I just wandered around. It was pretty hot so I only stayed an hour and a half, I didn’t see everything. Also only Hindus can enter the temples. As a Westerner and tourist, a few people wanted my photo, which was ironic, since I was there to witness them. The locals seemed lovely! One girl even gave me directions to Boudha stupa.\n\nThere are some brightly yellowed dressed Shadu (holy men) who will pose for money.\nThe row of temples had a lot of shiva phallic idols and animal statues.\nIt would be interesting to read and learn more about the symbolism.\nMy advice, read up before you visit.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "179A2ECDEF2EE3A877473B05CA883150", "name": "danzmerv", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/danzmerv", "username": "danzmerv", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/de/0a/default-avatar-2020-35.jpg", "contribution_count": 72, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 4375370, "location_name": "Padstow", "location_name_detailed": "Padstow, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-11-18", "published_at_date": "2019-11-18"}, {"review_id": 727034043, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r727034043-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Incredible, humbling, moving but be aware of closing time... of shoe racks", "text": "Incredible temple!!! i was travelling alone, arrived at 2pm and comfortabley spent 4 hours inside wondering around, taking in the atmosphere, visitings the smaller temples within the complex. I attended the main aarti and the aarti at some of other temples within and time flew by. I believe the aarti time inside the complex happens before the aarti across the river so you can visit both. note at the back of the temple you have an ariel view of the rituals on the river if thats your thing (personally i avoided that). \n\nHowever please be aware of the closing time, not of the temple but the shoe racks. After an afternoon of prayer like most i sat outside watching the children play and monkeys run havoc. I returned to the shoe rack at 6:40pm to find that it had closed and my hiking boots were locked inside. To cut a long story short, despite asking guards and pleeding with the security office no one was willing to open the shoe rack and return my shoes. And guess what, i had a flight the next morning. Despite asking people the opening time i received 3 different answers of 5:30am, 6am and 6:30am which didnt fill me ith confidence. The next morning i turned up at 5:45am, the shoe racks were open and i managed to get back my hiking boots. Note the temple is virtually empty at 6am and you can pray in piece rather than the scrum in the evenings. all in all this should be top any agenda.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "9E6520360499ED508884825793995528", "name": "bhadresh p", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/523bhadreshp", "username": "523bhadreshp", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/77/ae/default-avatar-2020-2.jpg", "contribution_count": 24, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-11-17", "published_at_date": "2019-11-17"}, {"review_id": 727009955, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r727009955-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Respectful ", "text": "Respectful on how to end one life in a open and holy place/ river.\n\nBachhareshwari Temple: do check it out too, as lot of traditional wood craving with eroticism, based on Hindu \"Bible\". \n\nWalk up to the hill and check out couple of Hindu temples too.\n\nBe aware of all the monkeys in group as they are aggressive.\n\nEnjoy enjoy", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2019-11-30"}, "reviewer": 